course: dictionary
lesson: 8123
title: Repeating patterns and words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Repeating means doing or saying something again and again. A repeating pattern goes over and over in the same order, so once you spot the part that repeats, you can predict what comes next.
explain: «In red, blue, blue, red, blue, blue, red, the repeating unit is "red, blue, blue", so blue comes next.» The unit is the chunk that keeps coming back. Find the chunk, and you can see the whole pattern.
explain: Repeating is not only for colours and shapes. In science, day and night repeat in a cycle, and so do the seasons. In music, a chorus repeats. Repeating also helps your memory: practising a spelling again and again helps it stay in your head.
fact: Repeating means doing or saying something again and again.
fact: A repeating pattern goes over and over in the same order.
fact: «A repeating decimal» has digits that go on again forever, like 0.333…
fact: The part that repeats is called the repeating unit. In red, blue, blue, the unit is red, blue, blue.
fact: Day and night repeat in a cycle, one after another.
exercise: In «red, blue, blue, red, blue, blue, red», what comes next? | green | yellow | *blue | red
exercise: In the pattern 1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3, 1, what is the repeating unit? | *1, 2, 3 | 2, 3, 1 | 1, 3 | 1, 2
exercise: «0.333…» is a repeating decimal. What does repeating mean here? | The number ends after three digits | It is a whole number | The number is very big | *The digits go on again and again forever
test: A game loop runs many times a second, repeating the same steps. What does repeating mean here? | Stopping and starting | Drawing a picture of a game only once | *Doing the same steps again and again | Doing each step one time and then never again
test: Why does repeating help you remember? | It stops you from learning | Repeating makes things go away | Repeating is only for maths | *Doing something again and again helps it stay in your memory
exam: In the pattern 2, 4, 6, 2, 4, 6, 2, what number comes next? | 2 | 6 | *4 | 8
